      "message": "feat(sim): dual contouring for the machined-stock mesh\n\nExtract the stock field's surface by dual contouring (Ju, Losasso,\nSchaefer & Warren, SIGGRAPH 2002) by default: one clamped QEF vertex per\nsign-changing cell, Hermite normals read from the crossing sheet, and\nridge-biased corner crossings replaced by the trusted planes around them.\nA pocket's floor/wall edge now survives (slot edge gap 0.0000 cells vs\n0.36 with marching tetrahedra; box volume 480.000 vs 472.3). Marching\ntetrahedra stays as IsoMethod::Marching and as the logged fallback for\nany dual mesh that is not closed.\n\nFixes #23\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
